  "goodToKnow": "Der Bahnübergang is a level crossing where a road crosses a railway, marked by the Andreaskreuz (St Andrew's cross sign) and often by Schranken (barriers) and flashing lights. Unbeschrankte Bahnübergänge without barriers still exist on rural lines. Deutsche Bahn is gradually replacing crossings with bridges and underpasses. Der Übergang also means transition. Plural: die Bahnübergänge."
